\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf7 <!-- GUIDANCE COUNSELOR CORNER -->
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 section\cf4  class="\cf6 gc-section\cf4 " id="\cf6 gc\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 gc-label\cf4 ">Guidance Counselor Corner</\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 h2\cf4  class="\cf6 gc-title\cf4 ">What Every Counselor Should Know and Share This Week</\cf5 h2\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 gc-body\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 p\cf4 >Ivy Day is the emotional apex of the admissions calendar, and counselors serve students best when they help families separate the emotional experience from the practical decision that follows. The right message for every student, regardless of outcome: the May 1 deadline is when the decision is made, not tonight. Comparing financial aid packages, visiting campuses, and speaking with current students all still lie ahead. Admission to an Ivy League school is a beginning, not a conclusion.</\cf5 p\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 p\cf4 >The Pell Grant crisis deserves dedicated counselor communication to families in the low- and middle-income brackets you serve. The shortfall will not affect current awards, but families planning for college after 2027 should know that the structural problems in Pell funding are real and unresolved. The most important protective strategy: encourage students to target institutions that meet 100% of demonstrated financial need through institutional aid, so that any federal reduction can be absorbed by institutional policy rather than family burden.</\cf5 p\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 p\cf4 >On the NIH crisis: for students interested in research careers in biomedical science, public health, or any federally funded research field, this is the moment to have an honest conversation about what research universities can actually offer right now versus what they offered two years ago. The ranking does not change. The available labs, funded projects, and faculty stability can change significantly. Counselors serving research-track students should build NIH funding status into their standard school research protocol.</\cf5 p\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 gc-share\cf4 ">
