\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf7 <!-- FOR FAMILIES -->
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 section\cf4  class="\cf6 families-section\cf4 " id="\cf6 families\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 section-label\cf4 ">What This Means For Families</\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 h2\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-headline\cf4 ">Your Action Guide \'97 Edition 2026-13</\cf5 h2\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 p\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-sub\cf4 ">Dr. Hurwitz's Analysis \'b7 March 23\'9627, 2026</\cf5 p\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 p\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-intro\cf4 ">This was the week of Ivy Day, a student loan restructuring, a Pell Grant emergency, and an NIH funding crisis. Here is what each story means for your family's planning.</\cf5 p\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-steps-grid\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-num\cf4 ">1</\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-title\cf4 ">Process Ivy Day emotionally, but make your enrollment decision analytically \'97 by May 1</\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-body\cf4 ">Whatever happened Thursday night, the enrollment decision comes on May 1. Compare every financial aid package. Visit every campus. Ask every financial aid office whether they will match competing offers. Make a deliberate choice, not an emotional one.</\cf5 div\cf4 ></\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-num\cf4 ">2</\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-title\cf4 ">Current borrowers: document your student loan status immediately and thoroughly</\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-body\cf4 ">The transfer to Treasury creates transition risk. Log into StudentAid.gov now. Download your loan balance, servicer information, repayment plan documentation, and any PSLF payment count. Do this before the transition creates confusion.</\cf5 div\cf4 ></\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-num\cf4 ">3</\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-title\cf4 ">If your student is Pell-eligible, build a financial aid plan that does not fully depend on Pell</\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-body\cf4 ">The structural shortfall is real. Target schools that meet 100% of demonstrated financial need through institutional aid \'97 so that a federal Pell reduction is absorbed by institutional policy, not your family's finances.</\cf5 div\cf4 ></\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-num\cf4 ">4</\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-title\cf4 ">Research-track students: ask about NIH funding status before committing to any research university</\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-body\cf4 ">Visit reporter.nih.gov. Search your target schools and departments. Ask your intended faculty directly about their current funding status. A department with funding uncertainty is a materially different environment than its reputation suggests.</\cf5 div\cf4 ></\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-num\cf4 ">5</\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-title\cf4 ">Use the enrollment cliff to negotiate \'97 regional institutions need students and their aid offices know it</\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-body\cf4 ">If you hold offers from regional or mid-tier institutions, this is precisely the moment to ask for improved merit aid packages. Enrollment pressure gives families real leverage. Use it politely, with competing offers in hand.</\cf5 div\cf4 ></\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step\cf4 ">
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-num\cf4 ">6</\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-title\cf4 ">Do not let the political narrative distort your evaluation of genuinely strong schools</\cf5 div\cf4 ><\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 fam-step-body\cf4 ">The enrollment data is clear: college remains valuable, and 19.4 million students are making that judgment with their choices. The crisis narrative is primarily about elite institutions. Your student's best path may run through excellent schools that are not in the headlines.</\cf5 div\cf4 ></\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 <\cf5 div\cf4  class="\cf6 advisory\cf4 "><\cf5 p\cf4 ><\cf5 strong\cf4 >Dr. Hurwitz's Bottom Line:</\cf5 strong\cf4 > This week asked families to hold two things simultaneously: the emotional intensity of Ivy Day and the structural seriousness of three systemic policy stories that will shape college financing and quality for years to come. The families who navigate this moment best will be the ones who separate the urgent (tonight's decisions) from the important (loan restructuring, Pell shortfalls, research funding) \'97 and act deliberately on both. That is precisely what this newsletter is designed to help you do.</\cf5 p\cf4 ></\cf5 div\cf4 >
\f1\fs32 \cf3 \

\f0\fs26\fsmilli13333 \cf4 </\cf5 section\cf4 >
